# Next.js Architecture

## App Router (`app/`)

- Colocate `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `template.tsx` per route segment.
- Keep `app/` thin: routing, layouts, and composition — delegate feature UI to modules.
- Import order: external → `core/` / shared → module-internal → types/constants.

## Feature modules (`src/modules/{feature}/`)

Each feature includes: `components/`, `hooks/`, `schemas/`, `services/`, `views/`, and optional `actions.ts`, `store/`.

| Folder | Role |
|--------|------|
| `views/` | Page-level View (RSC or client) |
| `hooks/` | ViewModel: state, React Query, Server Action calls |
| `services/` | Typed API/DB access; no UI logic |
| `schemas/` | Zod validation |
| `components/` | Reusable, stateless UI |
| `actions.ts` | Server Actions (`'use server'`) |

- No cross-module imports; shared code lives in `src/core/` or `src/lib/`.
- If the project has no `src/`, use the same module layout under `src/` or align `modules/` with the team convention.

## React Server Components

- Prefer RSC for non-interactive UI and data orchestration.
- Add `'use client'` only when required (hooks, events, browser APIs).
- Do not fetch in RSC directly — delegate to `hooks/` or `services/` (e.g. via `use()` where appropriate).
- RSCs stay pure: no `useState`, `useEffect`, or browser-only APIs.
- Avoid pulling client components into RSC files except as leaf children (hydration boundaries).

## Client components

- Small, focused; interactivity and hooks live in `hooks/` when non-trivial.
- Prefer data from RSC parents over client-side fetching when possible.
- Event handlers: `handle*` prefix; state names like `isOpen`, `hasError`.

## Server Actions

- Mutations and secure server logic in module `actions.ts` with `'use server'`.
- Validate with Zod inside the action.
- Prefer invoking from `hooks/` (ViewModel), not directly from presentational `components/`.
- Throw on failure; toasts and cache updates on the client (e.g. React Query).
- Do not call actions inside loops or inline conditionals — use event handlers.
- Avoid `redirect()` from actions triggered by client UI; use `router.push()` on the client when needed.

## React Query (in `hooks/`)

- Wrap queries/mutations in custom hooks: `use{Entity}{Operation}`.
- Do not call TanStack Query hooks directly in components.
- Co-locate query keys and fetch logic in the hook; type `data`, `error`, and variables.
